reason- able transferor would believe the transferee intends to be bound to the form. (c) A transferee will be deemed to have adopted a standard form as a contract if (1) the standard form is reasonably accessible electronically prior to initiation of the transfer at issue; (2) upon initiating the transfer, the transferee has reasonable no- tice of and access to the standard form before payment or, if there is no payment, before completion of the transfer; (3) in the case of an electronic transfer of software, the transferee signifies agreement at the end of or adjacent to the electronic standard § 2.01 SOFTWARE CONTRACTS"